 ### Detail Coefficient Representation
-This variant reduces memory usage to 4 bytes per voxel by distributing 32 bits across X, Y, and Z coordinates in a 12+10+10 split, supporting volumes up to $4096 \times 1024 \times 1024$ [S2]. It packs coordinates into two `GL_SHORT` values and unpacks them in a vertex program. For GPUs lacking bit shift operators, unpacking is emulated using multiplication by a fraction (via `floor` function) and subtraction [S2]. This approach trades computation for memory bandwidth efficiency, which is beneficial for large volumes [S2].
